I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment call. This node's `with` clause grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`, and the graph definition hasn't been updated to add `http-client`. The change would also send each customer's question to an external host outside the node's declared authority. The node below uses only the two granted interfaces. Once the graph's `with` clause includes `http-client` and the enrichment endpoint is reviewed, that addition can be made separately.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{conversation-context, response-result};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/tool-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(ctx: conversation-context) -> response-result;
}
```

